      "evidence_id": "pdfplumber:abstract",
      "source": "pdf_layout",
      "field": "abstract",
      "raw_text": "We present new constructions of succinct non-interactive functional commitments and arguments for circuits (i.e., P/poly), based on the SIS assumption without random oracles. For boolean circuits of depth. d and size. s over . l-bit inputs, we obtain - a non-interactive functional commitment scheme with . O(1)-sized transparentCRS,. O(1)-sized commitment,and. O(d)-sized op enings; - a non-interactive succinct argument (SNARG forP/poly)with. O(1)- sized transparent CRS, and. O(d)-sized unambiguous pro ofs. Here, . O(·)hides . poly(λ,logl,logs)factors. Moreover, both schemes sup- port fast online verification after a circuit-dependent pre-processing phase, and do not impose a bound on circuit parameters during set-up. Our constructions are simple, self-contained, and completely elementary: we rely only on simplealgebraicoperationsanddonotutilizecorrelation intractability, sum-check, or non-black-box use of cryptography.",
      "extractor": "pdfplumber_section_boundary"
    },
